# ============================================================
# Hit Your Mark Travel — line-ending policy
# ============================================================
#
# dist/ is build output. `astro build` writes it and the deploy uploads it
# to Hostinger byte-for-byte, so Git must not rewrite its line endings.
#
# core.autocrlf is true on the machine this repo is worked on, and Astro's
# compressHTML output contains MIXED line endings — a mixed file cannot
# round-trip through LF->CRLF->LF conversion, so Git saw ~86 dist files as
# modified after every single rebuild while `git diff --ignore-cr-at-eol`
# showed no actual change. Real edits were getting buried in that noise.
#
# -text switches conversion off entirely for these paths: what the build
# writes is what gets stored, and what gets stored is what gets checked out.
dist/** -text

# Source stays under normal text handling: it is authored with LF, and the
# CRLF working-tree copies round-trip cleanly because nothing here is mixed.
